Your first visit at Thrive Gonstead Chiropractic is your initial consultation, where we learn about your case and find out whether we can help. Your first treatment comes after that, on the same day or after X-rays if you need them.

At TGC, our focus is correcting subluxations (spinal joints that are not moving or sitting as they should) and the nerve interference they may cause (disruption to the nerve signals that pass through that area). Sometimes that nerve interference is the cause of your symptoms, and sometimes it is one of their effects. This guide walks you through each stage, so you know what to expect before you come in.

**Your visits at a glance**

1. **First visit:** consultation and physical examination. Complete the new patient form we send after you book.
1. **X-rays, only if your case needs them:** at a nearby facility, booked for you
1. **First treatment:** we explain your findings and, if you are ready, begin the first correction. It can be the same day if no X-rays are needed and you come in earlier in the working day. Otherwise, it is booked after your X-rays.
1. **Follow-up visits:** ongoing care, reviewed at each visit

## What should I prepare before my first visit?

Once you have booked, we will send you the new patient form, usually through WhatsApp. You do not need to search for it. Please complete it before you come in. It asks about your main concern, including how it started, what aggravates it, and what relieves it. It then covers your past medical history, your current medications, any serious illnesses or surgeries, and any other discomfort that may be connected to your main complaint.

Those answers give us the full picture before we see you, so the assessment and the plan we build with you fit your situation.

If you have had any previous X-rays or scans, please bring them along. If you have questions, bring them too.

## Step 1: The detailed history

The first part of your visit is a conversation about your health. We will ask you to describe the area that concerns you and when it started. We will also ask what makes it worse, what eases it, and how it affects your daily life.

We also ask about your goals. Imagine you did not have this discomfort. How different would your life be? Your answer tells us what matters most to you, so we can plan care around it. There are no wrong answers.

## Step 2: The physical examination

After your history, we move to the physical examination. It has five steps, and we explain each one before we do it:

1. Static palpation (feeling with the hands): we feel the spine and the muscles around it while you are relaxed
1. Motion palpation: we feel how each joint moves
1. Visualisation: we look at your posture and the way you move
1. Instrumentation: we use the nervoscope, a skin temperature instrument, as one part of the assessment
1. X-rays, if your case needs them

Tell us at any point if something feels uncomfortable. We will adjust what we are doing.

By the end of this stage, we will have a clear idea of whether you are in the right place and whether care with us is the right next step. If we find that you are better suited elsewhere, we will tell you honestly and refer you to the right provider.

## Step 3: X-rays, only if your case needs them

If X-rays are needed, we will send you to a nearby imaging facility and book the appointment for you. We also write the referral letter. All you need to do is attend the booked time and have your X-rays taken. If your first treatment is not on the same day, we book it for a time that suits you after your X-rays are done.

## Step 4: Your first treatment visit

Once we have your X-rays, we sit down with you to explain what is going on. We cover what the problem is, how long it has been there, what you can do to support your progress, and what we estimate your plan will look like.

If everything is agreeable and you are ready, we begin the first correction. This is a specific Gonstead adjustment, directed at the subluxation and the nerve interference that may be contributing to your symptoms. We explain what the adjustment involves before we begin, and you are never required to start before you are comfortable.

## Why do we correct one area at a time?

Gonstead care is specific. When we find more than one area that needs attention, we rank them by which correction would make the biggest difference, and we work on that one first. Then we move to the next, one step at a time.

This lets your body focus on one correction at a time, so each change is clear and easier to follow. In our clinical view, working through one correction at a time is the fastest way to move your progress forward, because your body can focus its response on one area before the next.

## What happens at follow-up visits?

A good correction often takes a couple of visits, so follow-up visits are scheduled accordingly. At each one, we repeat the examination, deliver the adjustment for the area we are working on, and explain what you can do between visits to look after your spine. We review your progress together and agree on the next step.

## Is chiropractic right for every symptom?

Not every symptom is a good fit for chiropractic care, and that is one reason we check your history carefully at your first visit. Some signs need a doctor's assessment first. The list below gives examples, not a full list:

- New or worsening weakness or numbness in the legs
- Changes in bladder or bowel control, even if they seem mild
- Sudden, unexplained weight loss
- New pain that starts after a fever or infection, which can point to a problem that needs medical attention

If any of these apply to you, please see a doctor soon. We are happy to talk through your next step, and we will refer you where needed.

If you are new to the method, start with [What is Gonstead chiropractic?](https://www.thrivechiropractic.com.my/blog/gonstead-chiropractic-explained). For local details, see [Looking for a chiropractor near me in Bandar Rimbayu?](https://www.thrivechiropractic.com.my/blog/chiropractor-near-me-bandar-rimbayu)

## Frequently asked questions

### Does it hurt?

No, getting adjusted does not hurt, and many people actually enjoy it. If you are already in a lot of pain, you may feel mild discomfort during an adjustment, but it is usually far less than what you are already going through. Tell us how you feel at any point, and we will adjust what we are doing.

### Is it safe?

Chiropractors use skill, not force or strength, to deliver specific adjustments, each directed at one identified area. Chiropractic care has a low risk profile, especially compared with more invasive forms of spinal care. However, all forms of spinal health care can cause adverse reactions in some people. That is why we take a full history and check for warning signs before any adjustment, and why we explain what to expect before you start.

### What should I wear, and will I need to change?

You will be asked to change into a gown for the examination. Female patients are always gowned. Male patients can remove their top if they are comfortable, and if not, we will provide a gown. Either way, we need to expose the spine for a clear view, and we will explain why before we begin.

### How many visits will I need?

It depends on your case, and we will have a clearer idea after your initial consultation and first treatment. In our experience, many cases show good changes within four to six visits, although that varies from person to person.

Ready to find out whether we can help? Book with us on WhatsApp at +6017 868 8789, or call the same number. Thrive Gonstead Chiropractic is in Bandar Rimbayu, and we will see you at the consultation.
